ation. The pH probe domain is tied directly to the controller ground, and the isolator's power output is short-circuited, so the pH EZO circuit will not power up or communicate correctly and the isolation purpose is defeated.\", \"confidence\": 0.85}], \"summary\": \"The pH isolator U3's V_ISO output (pin 12) is on the main GND net, while the matching EC isolator U4 drives a separate isolated supply net. This shorts the pH isolated supply to ground and breaks the isolation the specification requires.\"}",
